## Working alongside other agents

Other coding agents may be working on this machine at the same time. Coordinate through `agentlanes`:

1. Before editing, run `agentlanes list` to see what others hold.
2. Claim what you will change:
   `agentlanes claim <short-topic> --paths <files-or-dirs> --pid self --desc "<one line: what you are doing>"`
   If it prints `HELD` or `PATH HELD`, do not edit those paths. Pick other work, or wait with
   `agentlanes events wait --kind claim.done --timeout 600` and try again.
3. When finished (or when you give up), run `agentlanes release <short-topic>`.
   If you exit or crash, the claim ends by itself because of `--pid self`.
4. Run heavy commands (full builds, full test suites, browsers, model runs) through a slot:
   `agentlanes slot heavy 1 -- <command>`. Never start a second copy of a heavy command in parallel.
5. Claims expire after 120 minutes; run `agentlanes renew <short-topic>` if you need longer.
6. To wait for another agent, use `agentlanes events wait --kind <kind>` instead of sleep loops.
